$ goodfetch-collie usage --help
Shows, sets and raises the Limits of the user's Usage ledger, which hold every engine of the user

Usage: goodfetch-collie usage [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list   Lists every Limit of the Usage ledger, by scope, with the Usage charged and held against it in its current period and what is left
  set    Adds a Limit of the caller's own to the Usage ledger, which holds beside the others: the tightest one holds, so it can only lower what applies. Answers it with its Usage
  raise  Raises a Limit, in place of the ones of its scope, Usage kind, currency and period but a managed Operator policy's: a person's answer, asked at the terminal, and refused with `person_required` when stdin is no terminal

Options:
      --color <WHEN>  When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help          Print help

