Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>  The Run's ID

Options:
      --forwarded         Set by an engine that forwards the abort to the owner the Run index names (ADR 0031): an engine that does not own the Run then answers `run_not_owned` instead of taking its writer role
      --json              Prints the result as JSON
      --attached          Runs the call on an Attached engine in this process, even when a Daemon runs
      --daemon            Runs the call on the Daemon of the major, starting it if none runs; its refusal ends the command
      --require-verified  Exits 21 when the Run ended with a Verdict other than `verified`
      --color <WHEN>      When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help              Print help

$ goodfetch-collie run usage --help
Answers what a Run used, as the Usage ledger charged it: its model calls and tokens, browser time, proxy bytes, requests, paid solves and Paid fetches, each Limit that applies to it with what is left of it, and whether it is uncapped. An ended Run answers its report's Usage

Usage: goodfetch-collie run usage [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>  The Run's ID

Options:
