      --color <WHEN>  When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help          Print help

$ goodfetch-collie run progress --help
Reads a Run's progress: what it does and why it waits. Without `after`, it answers at once; given `after`, the position of the value the reader last read, it waits for a change and answers the latest value, so values in between are coalesced. The value whose `last` is true ends the sequence: the Run ended, and its `lifecycle` and `stop_reason` say how, or no engine works it (`writer: none`) until a start with its Run ID resumes it. A Run another engine works is read through that engine, the owner the Run index names, and one no engine works from its committed state; a read never takes the Run's writer lock. A Run ID the Run index does not list fails with `run_not_found`

Usage: goodfetch-collie run progress [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>  The Run's ID

Options:
      --after <AFTER>  The position of the value the reader last read: the answer is the latest value after it, once one comes. Absent, the Run's progress at once
      --json           Prints the result as JSON
      --attached       Runs the call on an Attached engine in this process, even when a Daemon runs
      --daemon         Runs the call on the Daemon of the major, starting it if none runs; its refusal ends the command
      --color <WHEN>   When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help           Print help

$ goodfetch-collie run report --help
Reads a Run's report: at once for a Run that ended, and at its end for a live one, which the read never ends. A Run another engine works is read through that engine, and one no engine works from its committed state, never taking its writer lock. A Run that has no live writer and has not ended fails with `run_interrupted`, whose `fix` names a start with its Run ID, and a Run ID the Run index does not list with `run_not_found`

Usage: goodfetch-collie run report [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>  The Run's ID

Options:
      --json              Prints the result as JSON
      --attached          Runs the call on an Attached engine in this process, even when a Daemon runs
      --daemon            Runs the call on the Daemon of the major, starting it if none runs; its refusal ends the command
      --require-verified  Exits 21 when the Run ended with a Verdict other than `verified`
      --color <WHEN>      When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help              Print help

$ goodfetch-collie run list --help
Lists the Runs of the Run index of the user and major, of either Product (ADRs 0031 and 0098): each row with its tags, Lifecycle, Verdict, Completeness, start and end, the engine that owns it while it is live, and its presence, a Run whose state is gone `missing` and one discarded on purpose `erased`, never left out. The engine filters by tags, the Recipe, Schedule, occurrence and trigger its reserved `goodfetch.` tags name, Product, each axis, start and end time, and a text found in its Run ID or tags, and sorts by the key given; Watch runs are left out unless `watch_runs` asks for them (ADR 0036)

Usage: goodfetch-collie run list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --completeness <COMPLETENESS>  Their Completeness: only Runs that ended have one
      --ended <ENDED>                When they ended: only Runs that ended match
      --lifecycle <LIFECYCLE>        Their Lifecycle
      --occurrence <OCCURRENCE>      The occurrence that started the Runs, by its ID
      --order <ORDER>                Which way, descending by default
      --product <PRODUCT>            The Product the Runs need (ADR 0098)
      --color <WHEN>                 When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
      --recipe <RECIPE>              The Recipe the Runs ran, by its name, as their reserved `goodfetch.recipe` tag names it
      --schedule <SCHEDULE>          The Schedule that started the Runs, by its ID
      --sort <SORT>                  What the rows are sorted by, when they started by default; rows that compare equal follow in Run ID order
      --started <STARTED>            When they started
      --tags <TAGS>                  Tags each row carries, every one of them
      --text <TEXT>                  Text found, ignoring case, in their Run ID or one of their tags, their Recipe's among them
      --trigger <TRIGGER>            What fired the occurrence that started the Runs
      --verdict <VERDICT>            Their Verdict: only Runs that ended have one
      --watch-runs                   Whether Watch runs are listed too; they are left out by default (ADR 0036)
      --json                         Prints the result as JSON
      --attached                     Runs the call on an Attached engine in this process, even when a Daemon runs
      --daemon                       Runs the call on the Daemon of the major, starting it if none runs; its refusal ends the command
  -h, --help                         Print help

