$ goodfetch-collie locator --help
Calls the catalog's `locator` operations

Usage: goodfetch-collie locator [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  click  Clicks the element the locator matches once it is unique, visible, enabled, stable and receiving the click (the guard, ADR 0019); a click that lands on another element is cancelled and sent again, until `timeout.action` passes. A click that starts a navigation of the page answers once that navigation's document committed or it ended without one, within `timeout.navigation` (ADR 0085)
  fill   Replaces the text of the field the locator matches, once it is unique, visible, enabled and editable, with text the page receives as typed input, until `timeout.action` passes. An input whose value a person picks rather than types (a date, a time, a month, a week, a local date and time, a colour or a range) has its value set, firing `input` and `change`, and a value it does not take fails with `invalid_params`
  press  Focuses the element the locator matches, once it is unique, visible and enabled, and presses a key or a combination on it as a keyboard does, until `timeout.action` passes. A press that starts a navigation of the page answers once that navigation's document committed or it ended without one, within `timeout.navigation` (ADR 0085)

Options:
      --color <WHEN>  When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help          Print help

