  -h, --help               Print help

$ goodfetch-collie key-value-store set-bytes --help
Commits bytes with their content type for a key in a live Run's Key-value store, replacing what it held: the last commit wins. Bytes over 1 MiB are kept as a file in the Run's folder, which its Checkpoints carry

Usage: goodfetch-collie key-value-store set-bytes [OPTIONS] --content <CONTENT> --content-type <CONTENT_TYPE> --key <KEY> --run-id <RUN_ID>

Options:
      --attempt <ATTEMPT>            The crawl attempt whose handler's `ctx.run` sets the bytes: the write is staged with the attempt and commits with it, a kept file written only then, or is discarded with it (ADR 0093). Absent, the bytes are committed at once
      --content <CONTENT>            The bytes, in Base64
      --content-type <CONTENT_TYPE>  Their content type, such as `image/png`
      --key <KEY>                    The key
      --run-id <RUN_ID>              The Run whose store it is
      --json                         Prints the result as JSON
      --attached                     Runs the call on an Attached engine in this process, even when a Daemon runs
      --color <WHEN>                 When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
      --daemon                       Runs the call on the Daemon of the major, starting it if none runs; its refusal ends the command
  -h, --help                         Print help

$ goodfetch-collie key-value-store delete --help
Removes a key from a live Run's Key-value store and answers whether it existed. Through a crawl attempt (`attempt`), the removal is staged with the attempt, and whether the key existed counts what the attempt staged

Usage: goodfetch-collie key-value-store delete [OPTIONS] --key <KEY> --run-id <RUN_ID>

Options:
      --attempt <ATTEMPT>  The crawl attempt whose handler's `ctx.run` reads or deletes the key: a read sees what the attempt staged, and a delete is staged with the attempt (ADR 0093). Absent, the call reads or commits at once
      --key <KEY>          The key
      --run-id <RUN_ID>    The Run whose store it is
      --json               Prints the result as JSON
      --attached           Runs the call on an Attached engine in this process, even when a Daemon runs
      --daemon             Runs the call on the Daemon of the major, starting it if none runs; its refusal ends the command
      --color <WHEN>       When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help               Print help

$ goodfetch-collie key-value-store keys --help
Sends the committed keys of a Run's Key-value store that start with `prefix`, in the order of their Unicode scalar values, in `$/key` notifications, one per credit granted with `$/credit`, then answers how many it sent. Takes no writer lock

Usage: goodfetch-collie key-value-store keys [OPTIONS] --follow --run-id <RUN_ID>

Options:
      --follow           Prints what the call sends as it arrives, until it ends
      --prefix <PREFIX>  The prefix of the keys it sends; every key when left out
      --run-id <RUN_ID>  The Run whose store it is
      --json             Prints what the call sends as one JSON object per line
      --attached         Runs the call on an Attached engine in this process, even when a Daemon runs
      --daemon           Runs the call on the Daemon of the major, starting it if none runs; its refusal ends the command
      --color <WHEN>     When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help             Print help

$ goodfetch-collie sample --help
Calls the catalog's `sample` operations

Usage: goodfetch-collie sample [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  echo  Repeats a text back to the caller

Options:
      --color <WHEN>  When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help          Print help

$ goodfetch-collie sample echo --help
Repeats a text back to the caller

Usage: goodfetch-collie sample echo [OPTIONS] --text <TEXT>

Options:
      --text <TEXT>   The text to repeat
      --json          Prints the result as JSON
      --attached      Runs the call on an Attached engine in this process, even when a Daemon runs
      --daemon        Runs the call on the Daemon of the major, starting it if none runs; its refusal ends the command
      --color <WHEN>  When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help          Print help

Deprecated since protocol 0.1, and removed no earlier than the next major: A sample entry, which the real catalog replaces.
